# Gaia 2.0 AI Rules (Updated)

## Source of truth
- Always consult Wiki SSOT first.
- Always read local numbered docs `docs/00_00...` through `docs/09_03...` for architecture/state.
- Use `README.md` for project positioning and messaging context.

## Core constraints
- Ruby version: 4.0.2 only.
- Rails backend uses PostgreSQL multi-DB and `db/structure.sql`.
- Sidekiq queue priority is strict:
  `uplink > alerts > critical > downlink > default > web3_critical > web3 > web3_low > low`.
- Firmware is C/STM32 domain; do not mix Ruby assumptions into firmware logic.
- Blockchain/web3 logic must stay in service layer namespaces.

## Development behavior
- Prefer minimal, precise changes.
- Do not rely on stale counts/statuses from old instruction files.
- If docs mark something as BLOCKER/open, treat it as unresolved by default.
- For frontend changes, follow `docs/04_04_Phlex_UI_and_Tailwind.md`.

## Validation
- Run RuboCop before finalizing.
- Run tests when environment dependencies (DB/network services) are available.
